From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:10:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] Round 10: Run the SIR series as a stencil on the (S, I)
 grid

Every SIR transition lowers 2S + I by one, so discovery numbers states
level by level and, within a level, by ascending S. Each generator column
(S, I) therefore adds the recovery source (S, I+1), the infection source
(S+1, I-1) and its diagonal in that order. Preparation verifies this
pattern and that each S row is a contiguous I range; the series vectors
then live on a zero-padded grid and each product row uses three
contiguous streams. Snapshot sums, moments, discarded weight and traces
gather in discovery order with the sink last. The round 8 slot kernel
remains the fallback, and the projection tests check both kernels
against the vendored solver bit for bit.

Workload: serial (96 SIR candidates, one worker), matrix API on both
sides, 11 samples.
Before median: 1.841 ms. After median: 1.597 ms. Speedup: 1.15x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
